DESCRIPTION:(2444) Lederle hides a magnitude 14.5 star\, seen from Visakhap
 atnam.\nThe predicted edge passes 2 km to the NNW\, so a miss is likely 
 — but a chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all
 .\nClosest approach 23:34:31 IST\, give or take 5 s. The star is 13° up i
 n the WSW · dark sky.\nIt fades 2.8 magnitudes for up to 4.3 s on the cen
 tre line\, and the path is 30 km wide\, give or take 18 km.\nFinder chart\
 , the map and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2026-09#
 2026-09-13-2444-lederle-717440
